    "report_the_discrepancy_to_the_supervisor": {
      "capabilities": [
        "email.send"
      ],
      "config": {
        "channel": "email",
        "effect": "notify",
        "idempotency_key": "container_no + batch_no + discrepancy_kind",
        "inputs": [
          "commercial_invoice",
          "certificate_of_analysis"
        ],
        "instructions": "Email the receiving supervisor naming the invoice number, the batch numbers affected and a description of what is wrong. This does not end the validation — we report it and carry on.",
        "is_terminal": false,
        "name": "Report the discrepancy to the supervisor",
        "outcomes": [],
        "payload_fields": [
          {
            "entity": "commercial_invoice",
            "path": "invoice_no"
          },
          {
            "entity": "commercial_invoice",
            "path": "line_items[].batch_no"
          }
        ],
        "recipients": [
          {
            "kind": "role",
            "role": "receiving_supervisor"
          }
        ]
      },
      "context": {
        "inherited": [],
        "local": [
          "[rule] The supervisor gets one email for the whole shipment, and that single message lists every affected invoice number and batch number together.",
          "[rule] The supervisor is chased the same way for a missing certificate and for a certificate that names a different batch, and the email names the batch and says what was found.",
          "[rule] When new paperwork lands, the process re-runs the whole check, but a corrected line only stops failing and does not create a new report for the same invoice and batch problem."
        ],
        "negative": [
          "The earlier discrepancy report is not retracted or replaced when corrected paperwork arrives; the same invoice and batch stay one issue, and the supervisor sees one email per distinct discrepancy rather than one per re-check."
        ],
        "provenance": [
          "2adcaf8f-d335-4299-b7c9-9d4b6d5eba74",
          "61422786-a65b-4038-8767-6a363efb1058",
